From 25d73e033b5116ca8bab8b03186a073db771342c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hhdy <103477680+hhdy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 20:46:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] regulator: scope boot proxy consumers to the regulator
 child node

ACK registers a whole PM8150 as one platform device, so the ROUND31
group-level helper could resolve only one proxy target per provider:
every child of the flattened pm8150-rpmh-regulators node voted on the
same regulator, which made it impossible to give the HOS4.3 L5 and L9
requests their own targets.

Introduce a child-scoped mapping: when the regulator child node itself
carries a "proxy-supply" phandle, the helper resolves the target with
of_regulator_get() on that child node (the pinned core already exports
this regulator-by-device-node API with full refcounting and
-EPROBE_DEFER semantics).  Children without a child-scoped proxy-supply
keep the ROUND31 group-level regulator_get() lookup unchanged.  Mixing
a provider-level and a child-level proxy-supply on one provider is
ambiguous and is rejected with -EINVAL instead of silently resolving.

A target that is not registered yet (or whose coupling is unresolved)
parks the request as deferred with no vote made; a late_initcall retry
gives it one more chance before the late_initcall_sync bulk revoke
drops it.  Each child keeps an independent consumer object, so
individual unregistration withdraws only its own votes.

The Kconfig symbol now depends on OF because the child-scoped path uses
of_regulator_get(), which has no !OF stub.

Signed-off-by: hhdy <103477680+hhdy@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/regulator/Kconfig          |   5 +-
 drivers/regulator/proxy-consumer.c | 250 +++++++++++++++++++++++------
 2 files changed, 204 insertions(+), 51 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
index 1eb68d402fe2..5ec1874c6b24 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/regulator/Kconfig
@@ -58,13 +58,16 @@ config REGULATOR_USERSPACE_CONSUMER
 
 config REGULATOR_PROXY_CONSUMER
 	bool "Boot time regulator proxy consumer support"
+	depends on OF
 	help
 	  This driver provides support for boot time regulator proxy requests.
 	  It can enforce a specified voltage range, set a minimum current,
 	  and/or keep a regulator enabled.  It is needed in circumstances where
 	  reducing one or more of these three quantities will cause hardware to
 	  stop working if performed before the driver managing the hardware has
-	  probed.
+	  probed.  Proxy targets are resolved from device tree "proxy-supply"
+	  phandles, either scoped to the regulator child node or declared on
+	  the provider node.
 
 	  If unsure, say no.
 
diff --git a/drivers/regulator/proxy-consumer.c b/drivers/regulator/proxy-consumer.c
index 1e0236cb04e7..380884892539 100644
--- a/drivers/regulator/proxy-consumer.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/proxy-consumer.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 /*
